

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                                PROMETEO







          Andrea Giovannetti
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Prometeo practiced his Druidism for months, but could make no 
significant progress.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Prometeo practiced his 
Druidism well, and even consulted an astrologer, but could not improve his 
Druidism.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer arrived.  Prometeo was instructed 
in Psychic Magic by Marlon.  Prometeo rehearsed and practiced his Psychic 
Magic and improved substantially.
  During fall, Prometeo cast a spell giving magical powers of oratory to 
Prometeo.
  Girard failed in his ineffectual attempt to cast an Oratory spell.
  In early winter, Prometeo boldly marched his command into Tesawa (#203).  
Viewing the western horizon, a man can see a Sea province known as Darkwood 
(#103).  It is said that no one reigns there.  It is known to be occupied by 
no races.


  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to Prometeo invaded the province 
of Tesawa, a Mountain area ruled by the provincial garrison commander.  
Prometeo was in command of the invading armies.  The defenders were led by 
the provincial garrison commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Tesawa (0203):

