  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with his warriors was Prometeo.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of the acting commander.
  Prometeo was not very fortunate this day, because the sun shone directly 
into his men's faces, giving the acting commander's men a small edge.  On 
the other hand his wise tactical maneuvers gave his side an undeniable 
superiority.
  Calling upon his arcane Spell of Oratory, Prometeo gave an inspiring 
speech to his army, which bolstered their morale.
  Across the whole front, the Veteran 231st Legion faced the 9th Legion.  
The 24th Heavy Cavalry outflanked the enemy and charged in with full 
strength.  In this engagement, the musicians of the 231st Legion asked 
permission to march in the van, and all were stirred by their martial music. 
The 231st Legion battled with the 9th Legion and thrust them back.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Prometeo as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 231st Legion annihilated the 9th Legion.
  Prometeo's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered Tesawa.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Prometeo for this year.


  Prometeo treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Prometeo treated with his 
ally Kwoth (#3).  Prometeo treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Prometeo 
treated with his ally Kahn (#6).  Prometeo treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Prometeo treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Prometeo 
treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Adhemar (#28) has just recently wandered into Tesawa from Amberleaf.
  Loviatar (#92) heard that an old buddy was trapping furs in Maicuru and 
left Tesawa to see her old friend.

  Cantia was plundered by the Werewolf, who stormed from out of the dark 
wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Prometeo's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 39 gold in revenue.  11 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 158th Dragons trained well and improved in quality.  22 gold 
was expended to maintain our armies.  Prometeo was left with 42 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tarsus
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I announced a call for volunteers in Alderwood and was able to 
enlist the 158th Dragons to fight for me.  I could not recruit more Dragons 
in Alderwood because the provincial maximum had already been recruited.
  During early summer, I dropped off the 257th Legion, the 232nd Legion and 
the 258th Legion in Alderwood for the provincial Dragon chieftain.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer came.  I attempted an 
illegal move.  I tried to use water-borne movement to move from Alderwood to 
Mare Imbrium, but my transport was insufficent for the task.  So, I 
practiced my Tactics for many weeks, but could make no significant progress.
  With the coming of the fall season, I tried to move from Alderwood to 
Darkwood, a non-adjacent province.  This is illegal!  So, I practiced my 
Tactics well but could not improve my skill in Tactics.
  During early winter, I tried to move from Alderwood to Waterford, a 
non-adjacent province.  This is illegal!  Instead, I worked on my Navigation 
but was thwarted in my efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Tarsus


From: Marlon
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to sweet spring.  Girard was magically charmed by 
me.
  With the advent of the early summer season Marlon's Bless spell fizzled 
and I was left with my face covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  In late summer, I tried to improve my Psychic Magic, but the task was 
beyond my aptitude.
  The summer surrendered to the fall.  I rode into Orielle.
  With the coming of the early winter season I moved into Macondo.  In my 
travels, I encountered no marauding monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


From: Tonto, Squire to Ishtar
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Ishtar was instructed in Druidism by Prometeo.  Ishtar 
practiced well and improved his ability in Druidism.
  The wet spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  Ishtar was tutored 
in Druidism by Prometeo.  Ishtar practiced for many weeks and his skill in 
Druidism increased.
  With the advent of the late summer season Ishtar journeyed to Orielle.  
Southeast of here lies the rich province of Mongu (#305), ruled by Bradipo I.
It is said to be a Jungle province inhabited by Humans.  Their Human 
warriors fight in the style of Legion and Light Cavalry.  Viewing the 
southwestern horizon, one can see a Jungle province known as Macondo (#205). 
It is said that Bradipo I is the ruler there.  It is known to be occupied by 
Orcs.  Their Orcish fighters array themselves in the style of Phalanx.  To 
the west there lies a Sea province known as Waterford (#104), an area of no 
races where no one rules.  Ishtar saw no marauding monster.
  In fall, Ishtar travelled to Macondo.  Southeast of here is Transylvania 
(#206), a Mountain province ruled by Bradipo I, where Dwarves dwell.  Their 
Dwarven warriors traditionally array themselves in the style of Axemen.  
Turning to the southwest, one can see a Desert area, which is known as Abu 
Matariq (#106).  It is populated by Humans and Bradipo I rules there.  Their 
Human warriors array themselves as Phalanx and Camel Corps.  To the west 
lies a Desert province named Bam Yanga (#105), populated by Humans.  It is 
ruled by Giovanna d'Arco.  Their Human fighters array themselves as 
Camel Corps.  Ishtar saw no wandering monsters.
  The fall season darkened into the stillness of early winter.  Ishtar tried 
hard to improve his Druidism, but he practiced in vain.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Ishtar


From: Berthier, Squire to Girard
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the early summer season Girard was instructed in 
Druidism by Prometeo.  Girard studied and practiced his Druidism and his 
skill in Druidism went up.
  In late summer, Girard was tutored in Psychic Magic by Prometeo.  Girard 
practiced his Psychic Magic and improved noticeably.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Girard failed in 
his ineffectual attempt to cast an Oratory spell.
  In early winter, Girard's attempted cast of the Skeletal Army spell was 
unsuccessful.

  Thy humble servant,   Berthier, Squire to Girard


